<title>EGYPT: Egypt local wheat supply reaches 1.3 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Egypt local wheat supply reaches 1.3 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's Minister of Supply and Trade Ahmed al-Gueily said on Tuesday that supply from locally produced wheat had reached about 1.3 million tonnes so far this year, state television reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Egypt is expected to harvest around six million tonnes of wheat in 1997.</p>
<p>Farmers have the option of selling to the government or to private sector millers.</p>
<p>The country usually imports about five to six million tonnes of wheat a year.</p>
<p>--Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290</p>
</text>
